+
+## Dirty-frame wake experiment
+
+The unselected `VOYAGER_EXPERIMENT_DIRTY_WAKE=1` control separates changed content from the normal animation clock on X11. The pinned GPUI core exposes optional dirty-frame registration and invalidation wake callbacks, with defaults that preserve other backends. The existing request structure remains unchanged. One closure factory supplies both requests with shared frame timing and deferred recovery state. A dirty-only request leaves the animation callback queue untouched. Reentrancy, inactive/thermal limits, forced recovery and pending presentation use the existing handler.
+
+The X11 callback queues one foreground task through weak state, callback and connection references. It clears its pending bit before delivery, rejects a dropped renderer and uses the same callback take/restore and recovery path as a normal refresh. Coalescing limits outstanding tasks, not frame rate. Native request frequency, response and resource measurements are required. Neither source preparation nor default-source compatibility establishes another platform's runtime behavior.
+
+The preparer now shares archive verification, patch application and source protection between checksum-pinned core and Linux packages. Cache paths include patch digests. Installed packages and older cache copies remain unchanged. Only exact previously generated Cargo configurations migrate automatically; personal or intervening edits are refused. The ordinary feature-disabled application excludes the diagnostic glyph module. The owner preview remains separate until the response and affected UX checks pass.
